SUMMARY:Stony Knob to Elk Pasture
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nNOTE THE CHANGE\n\nhere's the link
  to the location of the starting point:\n\n[https://maps.app.goo.gl/W9Fd5H
 RQJTS5zLJEA](https://maps.app.goo.gl/W9Fd5HRQJTS5zLJEA)\n\n(same link is a
 lso in my comment about change of venue)\n\nDM with questions\n\nwatching 
 the weather 👀\n\napprox 7 mile 1200 ft out and back on the MST/Shut In.
  three overlooks: Stony Bald\, Big Ridge\, Mills River Valley\, then on to
  Elk Pasture Gap (turnaround point)\n\nanticipated pace 2.5 ish mph\n\nwel
 l-behaved dogs are welcome!\n\nper previous hikes:\n\ngear up as appropria
 te\, trekking poles are an option. bring a snack as we'll take a break mid
 -hike. and plenty of water\n\nground rules: 1) if you sign up\, show up or
  change your status. 2 ) be sure you are in adequate physical shape to com
 plete the event. 3) show consideration toward all attendees. I hike for st
 ress reduction and want to keep it that way as much as possible\n\nLEGALES
 E\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, tran
 sportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for t
 heir own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physica
 l conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to one
 self and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group 
 can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. By signing up for this eve
 nt\, participant understands and agrees
