SUMMARY:4 Waterfalls\, darn tough hike
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nGraveyard Fields Upper Falls\, Low
 er Falls\, Yellowstone Falls\, Skinny Dip Falls.\n\n8 miles\, 1\,200+ feet
  of elevation\, darn tough trails\, pace approx. 2 mph. Must have the stre
 ngth\, stamina\, and stability (plus a fondness for alliteration) to compl
 ete safely the hike. Hiking poles\, hiking boots/shoes\, long pants recomm
 ended. This is not a dog friendly hike.\n\nStart at Looking Glass Overlook
  and take social trails up to and along Pisgah Ridge. Then take a social t
 rail down to Graveyard Fields parking lot. Graveyard Fields Trails takes u
 s up to Upper Falls\, then back down to Lower Falls. After that\, it's MST
  to the top of Yellow Stone Falls\, and MST takes us down to Skinny Dip Fa
 lls and back to our cars.\n\nWe'll **carpool** from the French Broad River
  Overlook. **Leave at 8:30 A.M.** Also\, it's Memorial Day\, so the Gravey
 ard Fields area may be crowded. Weather forecasts keep changing.\n\nThis h
 ike is an example of irrational exuberance!\n\n**Release of Liability:**\n
 The organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional guide. Th
 e function of the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up 
 or participate in this event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntari
 ly agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising
  from\, as a result of\, and associated with this event. In addition\, you
  acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: https://www.meetup.com/te
 rm
